      <h2 class="szekcio__cim">Compliance and proof</h2>
      <p class="szekcio__lead">
        In an audit, a client due diligence review or an insurance claim, what counts is not what
        we think of our own security but what we can prove on paper.
      </p>

      <div class="megfeleles">
        <article>
          <h3>Your data stays in Hungary</h3>
          <p>
            Data is stored in Hungary, on infrastructure we operate ourselves, at two Budapest
            sites, in ISO/IEC 27001:2022 certified data centers.
            Only authorized Triox staff have access to the infrastructure, to the
            extent required for operations. The exact terms are set out in the contract.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>GDPR-compliant data handling</h3>
          <p>
            Documented processes, a documented permission structure and up-to-date environment
            documentation. You are responsible for the content of the data and its lawful use—we
            are responsible for the technical and organizational conditions the data sits under.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Verified restores</h3>
          <p>
            A growing number of audits and regulatory reviews require proof that backups have been
            restore-tested. We do this in an isolated test environment, with an audit-ready
            report and a “passed / passed with recommendations for improvement / failed”
            rating.
          </p>
          <p class="megfeleles__hiv">
            <a href="/en/services/audit-restore-validation/">Audit Restore Validation →</a>
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Transparent reporting</h3>
          <p>
            Regular, automated infrastructure audits, change tracking and a resource report filtered
            to your own environment. If you are preparing for an audit—GDPR, NIS2, SOX or a client due
            diligence review—we go through it separately during the assessment, so the documentation
            is produced in the right form.
          </p>
          <p class="megfeleles__hiv">
            <a href="/en/sox-compliance/">IT operations under SOX →</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

